From: JeyKul <77121325+JeyKul@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:50:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 34/66] WIP: drm/amdgpu: Xclipse 920: Samsung sgpu ioctls, IB
 capture and patch knobs

Samsung's user-space driver (vulkan.samsung.so) calls three sgpu ioctls on
top of the amdgpu uAPI: SGPU_INSTANCE_DATA, AMDGPU_WGP_GATING and
SGPU_MEM_PROFILE_ADD. Answer them as book-keeping, so the vendor driver
runs on mainline amdgpu as a reference.

Debug module parameters for comparing drivers, all off by default:
ibdump=N captures the next N submissions (chained IBs, shader programs,
xcdumpva= memory) to debugfs xclipse_ibdump; xcpatch= rewrites register
values, xcrelmem= RELEASE_MEM fields and xcnop= packets in user IBs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
